  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Piloting an Insect Approach to Address Malnutrition and Food Insecurity</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Productivit&#xe9; du secteur priv&#xe9;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Am&#xe9;liorer la capacit&#xe9; des entreprises &#xe0; s&apos;int&#xe9;grer aux march&#xe9;s nationaux et internationaux gr&#xe2;ce &#xe0; des augmentations de productivit&#xe9; et &#xe0; des am&#xe9;liorations de la gouvernance d&apos;entreprise ainsi qu&apos;au d&#xe9;veloppement et &#xe0; l&apos;application de technologies et de pratiques de marketing modernes. Renforcer la capacit&#xe9; des entreprises et des associations professionnelles en termes de capacit&#xe9;s de gouvernance d&apos;entreprise et d&apos;application des meilleures pratiques et technologies pour accro&#xee;tre la production et la commercialisation de produits et de services. Cela comprend l&apos;adoption de processus de production efficaces, une productivit&#xe9; du travail am&#xe9;lior&#xe9;e, une gestion &#xe9;cologiquement rationnelle des ressources naturelles et le d&#xe9;veloppement de syst&#xe8;mes de comptabilit&#xe9; et de gestion qui peuvent aider l&apos;entreprise et le groupe industriel &#xe0; mettre en &#x153;uvre des normes commerciales, de travail, de produits et de processus qui am&#xe9;liorent la comp&#xe9;titivit&#xe9; des entreprises. Les programmes de d&#xe9;veloppement des capacit&#xe9;s des entreprises peuvent inclure des activit&#xe9;s qui aident les entreprises et associations appartenant &#xe0; des hommes et &#xe0; des femmes &#xe0; r&#xe9;pondre &#xe0; ces march&#xe9;s internationaux et &#xe0; cr&#xe9;er des alliances r&#xe9;gionales.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food insecurity is a significant global challenge, particularly in Madagascar, which ranks 119 out of 121 countries on the Global Hunger Index. Across the island, eight million people are undernourished, leading to early deaths, preterm deliveries, low birth weights, and irreversible cognitive and developmental delays for babies and children. To help alleviate this hunger crisis, the implementing partner has created a high-protein, insect-based instant porridge formulation for distribution by emergency and development food assistance programs. The porridge, which contains dried cricket powder as a key ingredient, may provide more protein and iron per serving than other commonly used nutritional supplements and can be baked into a cracker, among other preparations. Dried cricket powder is entirely local, inexpensive to produce, and aligns with Madagascan dietary preferences, which traditionally include edible insects. The implementing partner will scientifically test and fine-tune its instant porridge recipe to verify that it contains the ideal ratio and combination of ingredients and meets international nutritional and safety guidelines to qualify for formal accreditation as a nutritional supplement. As part of this award, the team will finalize a scale-ready version of its porridge and develop a commercial strategy to bring the final product to a national market. Once the dried cricket instant porridge formulation is accredited, global humanitarian organizations will be able to purchase, use, and distribute it to millions of people in need of nutritional supplementation.</narrative>
  </description>
